    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine how many distinct equilateral triangles in the plane of the nine-sided regular polygon \\(A_1A_2A_3A_4A_5A_6A_7A_8A_9\\) have at least two vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\), we need to analyze the possible configurations of such triangles.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the Possible Triangles\nAn equilateral triangle in a regular polygon is defined by three vertices that are equally spaced. We will consider all possible sets of three consecutive vertices, as these will form the most straightforward equilateral triangles within the polygon.\n\n### Step 2: Count the Triangles\nThe nine vertices can be labeled as \\(A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\). The possible sets of three consecutive vertices are:\n\\[\n(A_1, A_2, A_3), (A_2, A_3, A_4), (A_3, A_4, A_5), (A_4, A_5, A_6), (A_5, A_6, A_7), (A_6, A_7, A_8), (A_7, A_8, A_9), (A_8, A_9, A_1), (A_9, A_1, A_2)\n\\]\n\nThese are 9 possible equilateral triangles, each formed by three consecutive vertices.\n\n### Step 3: Verify That Each Triangle Has at Least Two Vertices in the Set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\)\nEach of the 9 triangles listed above clearly has at least two vertices from the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\). Therefore, every equilateral triangle formed by three consecutive vertices within the nine-sided regular polygon satisfies the condition.\n\n### Conclusion\nThe total number of distinct equilateral triangles in the plane of the polygon that have at least two vertices in the set \\(\\{A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_9\\}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
